ready: 1
kind: rule
id: agents.rule.fail-open
display_id: RULE-AGENTS-FAIL-OPEN
module: agents
title: A hook never breaks the agent
summary: Every failure, timeout, or missing piece yields an empty, non-blocking response with a success exit.
when: A hook handler meets any error, passes its deadline, finds Kernle uninitialized, or cannot reach the daemon for a write
then: It returns an empty response with exit status zero and the agent continues unchanged
constraints:
  - text: Only two responses may block a tool call, the Kernle-home write guard and a guardrail pause, and a pause lets the identical retry through.
    hard: true
  - text: A hook never contacts the network.
    hard: true
constants: [agents.const.hook-deadline]
